      <h1>Screenless fitness band: where NEXTBODY Hoop fits</h1>
      <p class="lede">People comparing WHOOP, Oura and other screenless trackers usually want sleep, recovery and load without a watch face. This page places NEXTBODY Hoop on that map using only numbers and limits already published on nextbody.ai.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>Who this category is for</h2>
    <p>A screenless band is a wrist tracker that keeps the display in a phone app. HOOP is one of those: no screen on the device, data in the NEXTBODY App. It is a fit if you want the following, and a poor fit if you want a watch face or a clinical instrument.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You would rather not wear a screen on your wrist for sleep and all-day tracking.</li>
      <li>You care about sleep staging, a readiness score and a daily training-load number — as wellness references, not medical advice.</li>
      <li>You may want an optional chat over your own account via MCP, instead of living only in dashboards.</li>
    </ul>

